    },
    {
      "title": "Trump signs executive order to rename Lake Ontario as Lake America",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/aug/27/trump-renames-lake-ontario-america",
      "description": "<p>Symbolic move to rename lake shared by US and Canada comes amid escalating trade war with northern neighbor</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/aug/27/cia-moscow-nato-ratcliffe-rutte-colby-trump-paxton-voting-latest-news-updates\">US politics live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Donald Trump signed an executive order on Thursday directing the federal government to rename Lake Ontario, making it Lake America, amid his escalating trade war with Canada.</p><p>The order directs federal agencies to adopt the name-change on US maps, documents and databases. But Trump has no authority to rename Canada’s portion of the lake, nor to compel Canada, international legal bodies, international mapmakers, or the rest of the world to adopt a new name.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/aug/27/trump-renames-lake-ontario-america\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-27T18:44:35"
    },
    {
      "title": "Trump signs order to rename Lake Ontario as Lake America amid Canada trade war – US politics live",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/aug/27/cia-moscow-nato-ratcliffe-rutte-colby-trump-paxton-voting-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>President hits out at Canada as he makes latest attempt to rename a landmark</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/2026/feb/17/sign-up-for-the-breaking-news-us-email-to-get-newsletter-alerts-direct-to-your-inbox?utm_medium=ACQUISITIONS_STANDFIRST&amp;utm_campaign=BN22326&amp;utm_content=signup&amp;utm_term=standfirst&amp;utm_source=GUARDIAN_WEB\">Sign up for the Breaking News US email</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>On Wednesday, Trump officially signed a proclamation on Wednesday that suspends higher tariffs on 300,000 metric tons of foreign beef imports for 90 days. </strong>This comes after backlash to the proposal – designed to lower grocery costs for Americans in the run-up to the November midterms.<br /><br />\n Several Republicans – in states with sizable cattle farming industries – have criticized the policy, saying it is a short term solution that will stymie ranchers’ ability to rebuild their herds.<br /><br />\n Four leading livestock and agricultural organizations also wrote a letter to the president on Wednesday urging him to reverse course.<br /><br /><strong>“Flooding the market with discounted foreign beef is not the way to rebuild the American cattle herd, strengthen food security, or lower grocery bills in a lasting way,”</strong> the groups wrote.</p><p>Donald Trump will begin his day in Washington, <strong>before traveling to Houston, Texas</strong> where he’ll headline a Republican National Commitee (RNC) fundraiser, and help boost <strong>Ken Paxton</strong> — the state’s attorney general and Republican nominee for Senate.<br /><br />\n A reminder that Paxton beat long serving Senator <strong>John Cornyn</strong> in the GOP primary earlier this year after receiving Trump’s endorsement. Paxton is set to face Democratic state lawmaker <strong>James Talarico</strong> in November.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/aug/27/cia-moscow-nato-ratcliffe-rutte-colby-trump-paxton-voting-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-27T21:07:15"
    },
